body:
**Context**
There is a new <ReplayPlayer> component and we should use it more often!

- New one: https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/blob/master/static/app/components/replays/player/replayPlayer.tsx
- The old one is: https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/blob/master/static/app/components/replays/replayPlayer.tsx

The new components don't work with mobile replays :(. I'm sure that none of them have been tested with mobile. The problem is that `replayContext.tsx` is where we instantiate `new VideoReplayerWithInteractions()`, but that hasn't been brought into the new system yet. So we'd need to instantiate that class (inside player/replayPlayer.tsx) and make the Video* class implement all the methods; luckily the Video class has a private `replayer` instance which can tell us the state, and emit events. We can write small adapters to get it done.

**Goals**
I'd say the goal is to get support for mobile first.
Afterwards, with one or many followup tasks we can refactor existing callsites to change from `replayPlayer.tsx` to become `player/replayPlayer.tsx`. 

For this one, the task is complete if the [replayPlayer story](https://sentry.sentry.io/stories/?name=app/components/replays/player/replayPlayer.stories.tsx) is able to load and play a mobile replay.

**Approach**
So we’d need to update: 
- https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/blob/7b3f7bd38503664b33afa7aa05eabca098a2c66f/static/app/components/replays/player/replayPlayer.tsx#L42-L54
- https://github.com/getsentry/sentry/blob/7b3f7bd38503664b33afa7aa05eabca098a2c66f/static/app/utils/replays/playback/hooks/useReplayCurrentTime.tsx#L13 and `useReplayPlayerState()` probably too. 

What i'd do first is to create an if-statement inside `player/replayPlayer.tsx`, `if (isMobile) { new VideoReplayerWithInteractions(...); }`. 
That'll cause a bunch of typescript issues because we'd be calling `didMountPlayer` and `didUnmountPlayer` with a new type of thing. 

So what i'd do to resolve the type errors is write `class VideoReplayerWithInteractions satisfies typeof Replayer` or something like that, so that the instances are interchangeable. This might cause the `satisfies` keyword to have an error because VideoReplayerWithInteractions is missing some properties & methods that Replayer has. But those are easily implemented. Something like:
```
class VideoReplayerWithInteractions {
  on(...args) {
    return this.replayer.on(...args);
  }
  off(...args) {
    return this.replayer.off(...args);
  }
}
```
